<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alsace-Lorraine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alsace-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> was the territory annexed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a> in 1871. It was administered as an imperial territory and became a lasting source of French resentment. France recovered it after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alsace-lorraine.jpg" alt="Alsace-Lorraine" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drawing created by David Liuzzo · Attribution · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dienstflagge_Elsa%C3%9F-Lothringen_Kaiserreich.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
